  "id": "Compound::DB00363 - Gene::11255",
  "verbalization": "Clozapine is implicated in the interaction with Chrm2, a G-protein coupled receptor, through multiple pathways that converge on Hrh3. The evidence suggests that Clozapine binds to Chrm2, which then participates in various receptor activities, including G-protein coupled acetylcholine or neurotransmitter receptor activities. These activities are ultimately linked to Hrh3, indicating a potential mechanism by which Clozapine influences Hrh3 through receptor-mediated signaling. The overlapping pathways highlight a common role of Chrm2 in mediating Clozapine's effects on Hrh3, suggesting a broad functional relationship. The integration of these pathways underscores the importance of Chrm2 in linking Clozapine to Hrh3, emphasizing a central role in receptor activity and signaling.",
